{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:23:07.485Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"8c6e5b530538bd2417954c22ca4fc076bc114fbbcd3f7dfd41b362352776d054","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina Kroll here's the list for Kwame's review. It covers tickets and feature requests found in #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's public Coastal digests and your Dec 2025 cutover note. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419: `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length (Moss cheat sheet). Note: Moss's 2 Nov digest attaches #4419 to a barge slip 7 schedule sync under \"Puget Sound Operations\". Please confirm which account it belongs to.\n- Ticket PD-8841: Gate 4B chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (your Dec 2025 cutover note).\n- Open friction, no ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (cheat sheet).\n- Open issues, no ticket number: Berth 2 yard map CSV import bug and Gate 4B printer mapping (your Dec 2025 note).\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (cheat sheet).\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B; engineering gave a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher (cheat sheet). No ticket number listed.\n- Patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 2 Nov digest). No ticket number listed.\n\nExcluded as other accounts: PD-4827, PD-4821, PD-4824 and #8812 (Saltmarsh and Pellow Home Living)."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
